  "title.m1a2_sep.blueprint.m1a2_sep": "M1A2 SEP Abrams Main Battle Tank",
  "description.m1a2_sep.blueprint.m1a2_sep": "The M1A2 SEP is the System Enhancement Package of the Abrams, with changes concentrated in digitisation and sights rather than outer shape. The 120 mm M256 smoothbore is fed by a digital ballistic computer; the gunner's primary sight carries a second-generation thermal imager, and the commander's independent thermal viewer (CITV) can search independently and hand targets to the gunner for hunter-killer engagements. Turret and hull front use composite armour with depleted-uranium mesh, with separately removable add-on armour on both flanks. Four crew, about 66 t combat weight, a 1,500 hp gas turbine, 67 km/h on roads and roughly 426 km of range.",
